      },
      "title": "Create the apiFetch helper function",
      "description": "## Create the apiFetch helper function\n\nSince our tooling calls the protected RetailZero API, we need to read the access token and add it to the `Authorization` header any time the tool is called. To get the session token, we will use the `getRetailZeroToken` helper function we just imported. We'll add some additional logic to another helper function called apiFetch that will called `getRetailZeroToken` and add the resulting token to the `Authorization` header.\n\n1. Select the **Insert code** link to implement this helper function:\n\n```ts\nasync function apiFetch(url: string, init?: RequestInit): Promise<Response> {\n  const token = getRetailZeroToken();\n  return fetch(url, { ...init, headers: { ...init?.headers, Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } });\n}\n```\n"
    },
    {
